{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.source_empirical_energy_limit","record":{"id":"scalar.source_empirical_energy_limit","kind":"claim","label":"The empirical adaptive energy converges to adjacent correlations","status":"unverified","source_id":"scalar-r6-source-empirical-energy-limit","locator":"EmpiricalEnergyLimit.lean:44–122; OAI.SKValueG.empiricalColumnEnergy_ae_tendsto","statement":"Fix K. Let f_j be measurable functions of coordinates z_0,...,z_j, with finite second moments, unit L2 norms and pairwise orthogonality for j<K. For a measurable sign S and each j<K, empiricalColumnEnergy converges almost surely to E[f_j S] E[S z_(j+1)] under independent Gaussian rows.","assumption_ids":[],"evidence_ids":[],"citation_ids":["scalar.source_empirical_energy_limit_lean_source"],"boundary":"Source-inspected statement with quantified guards retained. Authored proof correspondence, not elaborated dependency extraction or a fresh formal acceptance."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.source_empirical_energy_limit","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/69473417dc487cafa5e2e39b3168d2c4a8bffdad2e91b6e486de48f122dda071","roles":["mapped_claim"]},{"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/77f0cf29ab577b42d8caa5b2831ebfb1ca170d4b13c1ef6897cadc8e93c2a834","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]},{"stage":"expository","subgraph_ref":"sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json/support/0.3.1/9dd5536bc567fc55efaa864733bf89747cea0268a8a3865dec51ddd8e2a235dd","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]}],"direct_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/gaussian-empirical-limit","anchor":"gaussian-empirical-limit","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"}]},"aligned_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/gaussian-empirical-limit","anchor":"gaussian-empirical-limit","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\n<a id=\"empirical-gaussian-limit\"></a>\n\n#### 10.2.3 Why orthogonalization preserves the limiting correlations\n\nKeep $K$ fixed while $n\\to\\infty$. The strong law applies to the\nfinitely many needed products, which are integrable by Cauchy–Schwarz.\nThe empirical Gram matrix tends to the identity. Inductively in\nGram–Schmidt, every projection coefficient tends to zero and every\nremaining norm tends to one; hence\n$\\|v_{n,j}-\\widehat f_{j,n}\\|\\to0$ almost surely. In particular,\n$$\n\\langle v_{n,j},\\widehat S_n\\rangle\\to a_j:=\\mathbb E[f_jS],\n\\qquad\n\\langle\\widehat S_n,\\widehat z_{j+1,n}\\rangle\n   \\to b_{j+1}:=\\mathbb E[S z_{j+1}],\n$$\nwhile $\\langle v_{n,i},\\widehat z_{j+1,n}\\rangle\\to0$ for $i\\le j$.\nThe last limit uses precisely the fresh-coordinate cancellation stated\nat the start of §10.2. [Gram–Schmidt limits][scalar-gram-schmidt].\n\nExpand the revealed energy before taking its limit:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE_{n,j}={}&\\langle v_{n,j},\\widehat S_n\\rangle\n \\langle R_{n,j+1}\\widehat S_n,\\widehat z_{j+1,n}\\rangle\\\\\n&+\\frac{\\langle v_{n,j},\\widehat S_n\\rangle^2}{\\sqrt2}\n \\langle v_{n,j},\\widehat z_{j+1,n}\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nAll terms introduced by projecting away earlier directions vanish,\nas does the second line. The remaining product tends to $a_jb_{j+1}$.\nThus $\\sum_{j<K}E_{n,j}\\to\\sum_{j<K}a_jb_{j+1}$ almost surely.\nThis establishes the random-variable limit, but an expectation bound\nstill requires the next step.\n[Scalar implementation, empirical energy limit][scalar-empirical-limit].\n","span":{"start_byte":176617,"end_byte":178132,"start_line":3769,"end_line":3804},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=gaussian-empirical-limit","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=gaussian-empirical-limit"}],"lenses":{"prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=scalar.source_empirical_energy_limit&assumptions=true","consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=scalar.source_empirical_energy_limit&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&node=scalar.source_empirical_energy_limit&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&node=scalar.source_empirical_energy_limit&relation=prerequisites"},"relations":[{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/edges/%5B%22scalar.source_predictable_lower%22%2C%22scalar.source_empirical_energy_limit%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.source_predictable_lower","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2